// Placing is a round brush like digging: a radius-2 brick brush on the floor fills the open half
// of a 13-cell disc (9 cells; the 4 below the floor line are rock already).
map
###############################
#.............................#
#.............................#
#.............................#
#.............................#
#.....@.......................#
###############################
end
give Brick 40
brush 1 2
place 2 6 0 Brick
expect 3 static:StoneBrick == 9
expect 3 is:6,-2,StoneBrick == 1
expect 3 is:4,0,StoneBrick == 1
expect 3 is:8,0,StoneBrick == 1
expect 3 is:6,-3,StoneBrick == 0
// bricks come 4 cells to an item: 9 cells use 3 bricks
expect 3 inv:Brick == 37
// a second stroke in open air touching the first fills only what can rest on something
place 10 9 -2 Brick
expect 12 is:9,-2,StoneBrick == 1
expect 300 static:StoneBrick >= 15
